        "## 10.17 Worked calculation: one softmax gradient\n",
        "\n",
        "Suppose a three-class model gives logits\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "z=(2,1,0).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Then\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "p=\\operatorname{softmax}(z)\n",
        "=\\frac{1}{e^2+e+1}(e^2,e,1).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "If the true class is $1$ using zero-based indexing, then $e_y=(0,1,0)$ and\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\nabla_z\\ell=p-e_y.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Using approximate values,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "p\\approx(0.665,0.245,0.090),\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "so\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\nabla_z\\ell\\approx(0.665,-0.755,0.090).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The negative entry for the true class means gradient descent will increase the true-class logit.  The positive entries for the other classes mean gradient descent will decrease the competing logits.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 10.18 Neural networks versus classical text classifiers\n",
        "\n",
        "The table summarizes important contrasts.\n",
        "\n",
        "| Model | Representation | Decision function | Strength | Limitation |\n",
        "|---|---|---|---|---|\n",
        "| Naive Bayes | counts | log posterior score | simple probabilistic model | strong independence assumption |\n",
        "| Logistic regression | fixed feature vector | linear logits | interpretable and convex | depends on chosen features |\n",
        "| Averaged embeddings | trainable token vectors | linear or nonlinear logits | learns representation | weak treatment of word order |\n",
        "| RNN/LSTM | sequence of embeddings | recurrent hidden state | uses order | harder to parallelize |\n",
        "| Transformer | sequence of contextual embeddings | attention-based maps | long-range interactions | expensive and data-hungry |\n",
